rgia O'Keeffe Museum. [L.2004.30.1]","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Medium and Dimensions","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_medium_dims"}],"content":"Pastel on paper, 27 ¾ x 43 ¾ inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Private Collection","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Artist(s)","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_artist"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"The Black Place III, 1945","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Pastel on paper","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Two large sets of rolling hills dip down into a valley, creating a series of U-shapes throughout the center of the composition. The leftmost hills are darker, almost black, and a line through the valley's center shows where the two hill formations meet. Hints of red and yellow add depth to the landscape.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Whitney Archive indicates, \"Exam. at Amer. Place, March, 1946.. . . No signature.\" O'Keeffe wrote: \"I have been working on a pastelle of the Black Place\" (O'Keeffe to Maria Chabot, 3 December 1945). (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{